-* https://go.dev/[Go] - To build the plugin binary. Use the version of Go specified in `go.mod`.
+The repository's link:flake.nix[`flake.nix`] and link:flake.lock[`flake.lock`]
+pin the complete development environment, including Go, Packer, GoReleaser,
+`actionlint`, and the standard command-line tools used by the Makefile. Install
+https://nixos.org/download/[Nix] with flakes enabled, then run:
+
+[source,sh]
+----
+nix develop
+# Run these commands inside the development shell.
+go mod download
+go mod download -modfile=tools/go.mod
+----
+
+Amp Orbs run link:.agents/setup[`.agents/setup`] automatically. The setup is
+noninteractive and installs the same locked toolchain and Go modules. No
+credentials are needed to build, generate documentation, lint, or run unit
+tests.
+
+If Nix is not used, install a Go 1.27 toolchain and a compatible Packer release
+manually. The Makefile continues to pin Go-based lint and documentation tools
+through the repository's Go modules.
+
+== Development Checks
+
+Run the same checks as pull-request validation before submitting a change:
+
+[source,sh]
+----
+make build
+make test
+make plugin-check
+make lint
+make check-generated
+goreleaser check
+actionlint
+----
+
+`make fmt` applies the configured Go formatters. Generated documentation and
+code produced by `make generate` must be committed.
 
