+= Development Secrets
+
+No secrets are required for `make build`, `make test`, `make lint`,
+`make generate`, `make plugin-check`, or `goreleaser check`.
+
+== Oxide Acceptance Tests
+
+Tests that create or inspect Oxide resources require:
+
+* `OXIDE_HOST` and `OXIDE_TOKEN`, or an `OXIDE_PROFILE` understood by the Oxide
+  Go SDK.
+* `OXIDE_PROJECT`, which defaults to `packer-acc-test`.
+* `OXIDE_BOOT_DISK_IMAGE_NAME` for builder tests, which defaults to `noble`.
+* `OXIDE_INSECURE_SKIP_VERIFY` only when explicitly needed for a development
+  endpoint.
+
+Run them with `make testacc`. They may create billable or persistent resources
+and can take up to two hours. Store credentials in Amp project secrets or your
+local secret manager; do not commit them or place them in `flake.nix`.
+
+The manually triggered `Test Example Configuration` GitHub workflow expects
+repository or environment secrets named `OXIDE_HOST` and `OXIDE_TOKEN`.
+
+== Releases
+
+The manually dispatched release workflow uses GitHub's ephemeral
+`GITHUB_TOKEN`; maintainers do not need to configure a personal access token.
+The repository's Actions settings must permit that token to write repository
+contents so the workflow can create the tag and release and upload artifacts.
